  "period_note": "Year-end (31 December 2021) position, SOLO basis, primarily from the bank's own audited Balance Sheet, Profit and Loss Account and the 'Highlights on the overall activities of the bank' annexure in that year's own annual report. SBAC Bank Investment Limited (a brokerage/investment subsidiary) first appears as a consolidated subsidiary around this period; both Solo and Consolidated financial statements and 'Highlights' annexures are published from this year on. This dataset uses SOLO throughout per the standing methodology; Solo total assets (98,172,322,252) is slightly HIGHER than Consolidated (97,813,747,714) for FY2021 -- plausible given the subsidiary is a small, non-lending entity and intercompany placements/investment-in-subsidiary eliminations on consolidation can net to a small reduction. Total loans and advances are identical Solo vs Consolidated (65,955,681,066) confirming the subsidiary does not lend. 'Other expenses' rose from 394,777,039 (2020) to 1,503,159,089 (2021), a 281% jump, not separately explained in extractable text. Total Capital and CRAR are directly reported and reconcile (10,834.47/77,701.66=13.943%=13.94%, matching the narrative-stated Solo CRAR exactly). A Tier-I/Tier-II split specific to Solo was not found in extractable text (only a Solo-vs-Consolidated TOTAL capital comparison, and a Consolidated-basis CET1/Tier2 ratio elsewhere), so the split is left as a gap rather than mixing Solo totals with Consolidated ratios.",
